{
 "_comment": "Hermes Agent (METRICS 4.15). `home` plays the Hermes home; `discover` lists the log files of its log folders. Feed the files of `order` (modification times `mtimes`) to one parser state per log folder, with wall times in `timeZone`, and the shared dedupe set; `sets` gives, per log folder, its malformed API-call lines and one agent per session id (the empty id is the agent of lines without a session tag; agent id = absolute folder path + '#' + id), in the order agents first appear. `traces` give one session's phase after feeding a file up to and including physical line `afterLine`, after the files before it in `order`. `wallTimes` convert a record line's timestamp in a zone (null: not a record line). `homes` resolve the Hermes home from an environment. `rotation` replays a log folder with real renames: `append` writes `lines` (each followed by a newline) or raw `text` to a file and sets its modification time, `rename` and `delete` change files, `read` reads every file of the folder from the offset its identity reached and checks every response key emitted so far and the listed agents. `runtimeConfigs` give config.yaml texts and whether they select the Codex runtime; `agentConfigs` give texts and the two scalars of their `agent` block (EXECUTION-MODES). `home` also holds `state.db`, whose sessions give the agents' session-current effort. `codexRuntime` replays a Hermes home (folder `home`, with the profile `p`): `write` sets a file's text (`size`: padded with `#` to that many bytes) and modification time, `remove` deletes it, `append` works like the rotation's, and `read` checks the config.yaml of every log folder, then reads its new lines, and checks each listed log folder's switch, every response key emitted so far and the listed agents.",
